"""Original engineering scenarios with explicit diagnostic evidence."""
ITEMS=[]
def family(options, rows):
    assert len(options)==len(rows)==4
    for k,(stem,why) in enumerate(rows):ITEMS.append((stem,[options[k]]+[v for j,v in enumerate(options) if j!=k],why))
family(['Correct the token audience','Refresh the signing-key cache','Correct the verifier clock','Restore the required permission'],[
('An API rejects a signed, unexpired token with aud=inventory. The requested API expects aud=payroll, and the issuer and signature are trusted. Which correction addresses the rejection?', 'The audience must identify the intended recipient. A valid signature does not authorize replay to a different API.'),
('After an identity provider rotates its signing key, one service reports an unknown key identifier. Other services validate the same issuer’s new tokens successfully. Its issuer configuration is unchanged. What should be checked first?', 'The verifier may have stale signing-key metadata. Changing the token audience would not resolve an unknown signing key.'),
('A token is valid from12:00 to12:10 UTC. The identity provider and other systems show12:04, but one verifier shows12:24 and rejects it as expired. Which correction targets the evidence?', 'Correct the verifier’s time synchronization. Extending token validity would mask the clock problem and increase exposure.'),
('A service successfully validates identity, signature, audience and expiry, then logs an authorization failure for a newly required operation. Its role lacks that operation. Which change fits?', 'Grant only the required operation through the approved permission model. Authentication checks have already passed and do not supply missing authorization.')])
family(['Repair the federation trust','Remove an obsolete role grant','Renew the device attestation','Revoke the compromised credential'],[
('A partner’s assertions are rejected after its approved issuer identifier changed. User accounts and entitlements are unchanged, and validation fails before permission evaluation. Which configuration needs review?', 'Federation trust must recognize the authorized issuer and associated validation metadata. Adding roles cannot fix a failed issuer trust check.'),
('An employee moved from finance to logistics but still has finance approval authority alongside the new role. Which lifecycle action addresses this accumulated privilege?', 'Remove the obsolete grant after verifying current duties. A new identity proofing step does not remove old permissions.'),
('Conditional access denies a managed laptop because its integrity evidence is older than the policy permits. The user has passed authentication and has the correct role. What should be refreshed?', 'Renew the device posture or attestation evidence through the managed process. Additional user privileges do not satisfy a device-condition requirement.'),
('A service key is confirmed exposed. A replacement has been securely deployed and verified, but the old key still authenticates. What lifecycle action remains necessary?', 'Revoke the exposed credential after the replacement is working. Merely creating a new key does not invalidate the old one.')])
family(['Constrain the resource scope','Shorten the privilege duration','Require a second approval','Record the privileged session'],[
('A maintenance role is active for only fifteen minutes and requires approval, but it can modify every tenant instead of the one authorized for the ticket. Which control dimension needs correction?', 'Reduce resource scope to the authorized tenant. A short lifetime still permits excessive actions during that interval.'),
('A role reaches only the approved server, but elevation remains active for weeks after a ten-minute maintenance task. Which dimension should be reduced?', 'Limit elevation duration and expire it when no longer needed. Resource scoping does not address unnecessary time at privilege.'),
('A high-impact change already has narrow scope and automatic expiry. Policy requires independent authorization, but the operator can self-approve it. Which control is missing?', 'An independent second approval enforces the stated separation of duties. Session recording documents actions but does not authorize them.'),
('A privileged action is properly scoped, time-limited and approved. Investigators still cannot reconstruct what the operator did. Which added capability answers that need?', 'An appropriate protected session record supports investigation. Narrow permissions alone do not preserve a history of actions.')])
family(['Separate authentication from access','Bind the assertion to its recipient','Validate current account status','Use an independent recovery path'],[
('A help desk assumes that a successful login means a user may approve payments. The application has not evaluated payment authority. Which design distinction resolves this mistake?', 'Authentication establishes identity; authorization determines permitted actions. A valid identity does not confer every business permission.'),
('A signed federated assertion intended for one service is accepted by another. The issuer is trusted by both. Which validation requirement closes this substitution gap?', 'Validate recipient or audience restrictions as well as signature and issuer. Shared trust in an issuer does not make assertions interchangeable.'),
('A local application keeps authorizing a user after the organization disables the user’s account upstream. Which integration property should be corrected?', 'Current account and session status must propagate into access decisions. An earlier valid login cannot justify indefinite access after deactivation.'),
('Administrators cannot recover a failed identity service because their only administrative login depends on that same service. Which design change breaks the circular dependency?', 'A controlled independent emergency path supports recovery when the primary identity dependency fails. It needs strong protection and auditing.')])
family(['Application execution control','Endpoint behavioral detection','Host network filtering','Browser execution isolation'],[
('A kiosk must execute only a small approved set of signed applications. The immediate requirement is to prevent other executables from starting. Which endpoint capability fits?', 'Application control enforces permitted execution. Behavioral detection may identify malicious activity after execution begins.'),
('A workstation runs an approved interpreter that begins unusual child-process and credential-access behavior. The team needs to detect and investigate that behavior. Which capability is most direct?', 'Endpoint behavioral detection observes process activity, including abuse of approved tools. An allowlist alone may permit the interpreter.'),
('A server must accept management connections only from a dedicated administration subnet, including when upstream routing changes. Which host control enforces this local network boundary?', 'A host firewall can restrict allowed source networks and services at the server. Browser isolation does not enforce server management ingress.'),
('Staff must view untrusted external websites while keeping website execution separated from their ordinary workstation environment. Which capability addresses that requirement?', 'Browser isolation separates execution of untrusted web content. A host network rule alone does not provide that execution boundary.')])
family(['Drop unnecessary capabilities','Remove the daemon socket mount','Make application files read-only','Set a bounded resource quota'],[
('A container runs as a non-root user but retains kernel capabilities its application never uses. Which hardening change removes this unnecessary privilege?', 'Drop capabilities that the workload does not require. Non-root execution alone does not establish that every assigned capability is necessary.'),
('A monitoring container can reach the host’s container-management socket even though it needs only exported metrics. Which change removes the high-impact management path?', 'Remove the unnecessary socket exposure. A read-only filesystem mount does not make the management API itself read-only.'),
('An application needs to read packaged code but write only to one temporary directory. Which filesystem change limits unexpected alteration of its code?', 'Make application files read-only and provide only the necessary writable location. Resource quotas address consumption rather than file modification.'),
('A defective container consumes nearly all host memory, starving unrelated services. Which container setting most directly limits this failure’s resource impact?', 'A suitable memory quota bounds consumption. Read-only files do not limit how much memory the process allocates.')])
family(['Correct the certificate name','Install the required chain','Align supported TLS parameters','Renew the expired certificate'],[
('A client requests api.example.invalid but receives a currently valid certificate naming files.example.invalid. Trust-chain validation succeeds. What needs correction?', 'The certificate identity must match the requested service. Trust in the issuer does not cure a hostname mismatch.'),
('A newly deployed server presents its leaf certificate without the required intermediate. Clients trust the root but cannot build a path to it. What should the server administrator supply?', 'Supply the appropriate intermediate chain so clients can build the trust path. A new hostname does not resolve a missing issuer link.'),
('A TLS handshake fails before certificate verification. Logs show the client and server have no mutually supported protocol parameters. What should be aligned within the approved security baseline?', 'A compatible approved TLS configuration is required for negotiation. Certificate renewal cannot create a shared protocol or cipher configuration.'),
('A certificate’s validity ended yesterday. The service name and issuer chain are correct and clients have accurate clocks. Which action addresses the specific failure?', 'Renew and deploy a valid certificate through the authorized process. Changing the trust store is not a proper cure for expiry.')])
family(['Check the authorized sending hosts','Verify the message-domain signature','Inspect the signed DNS response','Validate the TLS peer identity'],[
('A receiver needs to know whether an SMTP sender is authorized to use the envelope MAIL FROM domain. Which mechanism’s evidence should it inspect?', 'SPF checks the sending host against the domain’s published authorization. It does not sign the message content.'),
('A mail gateway needs to verify a domain’s cryptographic responsibility for selected headers and the covered message body. Which evidence addresses that question?', 'DKIM verifies a signature associated with a signing domain. A successful signature does not by itself establish that the visible author is trustworthy.'),
('A resolver needs to validate the origin and integrity of DNS data using the DNSSEC trust chain. Which evidence is relevant?', 'DNSSEC validation checks signed DNS data and its trust chain. It does not provide confidentiality for ordinary DNS queries.'),
('An application connects to a remote HTTPS endpoint and must establish that the encrypted channel terminates at the intended service. Which validation is needed?', 'TLS peer identity validation uses the appropriate certificate identity and trust checks. Email-domain authorization is unrelated to this channel.')])
family(['Correct the ordered filter rule','Restore the missing return route','Move the observation point','Tune the validated detection rule'],[
('A firewall uses first-match processing. An early broad deny covers the approved management subnet, so a later narrow allow never matches. Which correction addresses the observed block?', 'Correct rule ordering or scope so the approved flow reaches its intended decision. A detection-rule change does not alter the access filter.'),
('A request reaches a service through a tunnel, but packet captures show replies leaving through an unrelated default path. The filter permits both directions. What should be corrected?', 'Restore the proper return route so replies use the intended path. Changing an already permissive filter does not fix asymmetric routing.'),
('A sensor sees only internet-bound traffic, but the required detection concerns communication between two internal workload segments. Which change directly gives it the missing visibility?', 'Place observation where the relevant east-west traffic can be seen. A more sensitive rule cannot detect packets the sensor never receives.'),
('A sensor captures the relevant traffic correctly, but a rule consistently flags an approved application behavior as malicious. Analysts have verified the behavior and its scope. Which action addresses the false positives?', 'Tune the validated rule or scoped exception while preserving relevant coverage. Moving the sensor does not correct faulty classification of traffic it already sees.')])
family(['Authenticate firmware updates','Detect unauthorized firmware change','Recover a trusted firmware image','Protect the recovery trust anchor'],[
('A device accepts firmware only after verifying that an update is authorized and intact. Which platform-resilience function is implemented?', 'Authenticated update protects firmware integrity before installation. Recovery restores a trusted state after a failure or corruption.'),
('A platform compares critical firmware against trusted integrity expectations and reports unauthorized change. Which resilience function is this?', 'Detection identifies a departure from the authorized state. Reporting corruption alone does not restore the firmware.'),
('After confirmed firmware corruption, a platform uses an authorized recovery mechanism to restore valid critical code. Which resilience function is being exercised?', 'Recovery returns critical firmware to a state of integrity. Preventive verification alone cannot repair existing corruption.'),
('A recovery design stores its trusted verification basis where ordinary compromised software can overwrite it. Which design element most needs protection?', 'The recovery trust anchor must resist the compromise it is meant to recover from. A backup image is insufficient if its trust basis can also be replaced.')])
family(['A protected signing-key service','A hardware-rooted device measurement','An isolated execution environment','An encrypted storage device'],[
('A signing service must perform private-key operations while keeping the signing key inside a dedicated protected cryptographic boundary. Which technology role best fits?', 'A protected signing-key service backed by an appropriate HSM keeps key operations inside that boundary. Disk encryption alone does not provide that operational isolation.'),
('A remote verifier needs trustworthy evidence about a device’s boot measurements, rooted in protected hardware state. Which capability is most relevant?', 'Hardware-rooted measurement and attestation support verification of device state. Encryption of stored files does not attest boot integrity.'),
('A workload must process sensitive data inside a hardware-supported protected execution boundary. The concern is exposure during processing, not only on disk. Which capability fits?', 'An isolated execution environment can protect selected data and code in use within its threat model. Storage encryption protects a different state.'),
('The primary threat is physical theft of a powered-off drive. Which capability directly protects the stored contents when its keys remain protected?', 'Storage encryption addresses confidentiality of data on the stolen drive. It does not automatically protect plaintext on a running compromised host.')])
family(['Use passive network observation','Test changes with control engineers','Restrict the permitted OT flows','Plan supported component replacement'],[
('A fragile industrial controller has not been assessed for active scan safety. The immediate need is to learn its normal communications without probing it. Which method fits?', 'Passive observation collects existing traffic without sending active probes. Even passive deployment should respect operational and safety constraints.'),
('A vendor provides a patch for a safety-relevant controller. Its effect on timing and process behavior has not been validated in the site configuration. Which step should precede production rollout?', 'Test the change with operational experts in an appropriate environment. Ordinary IT patch success does not prove process safety or timing compatibility.'),
('An unsupported controller must remain in service during an approved replacement interval. It needs communication with only two known systems. Which compensating boundary reduces unnecessary reachability?', 'Restrict flows to the documented operational requirements. Monitoring alone would not prevent unrelated systems from reaching it.'),
('A legacy component has no supported update path and its residual risk cannot remain acceptable indefinitely. A temporary segmentation plan is already approved. Which lifecycle action addresses the enduring problem?', 'Plan replacement with a supported component. Compensating controls can reduce exposure temporarily but do not restore vendor support.')])
family(['Preserve the validated safety response','Schedule a controlled maintenance window','Verify the redundant control path','Document the constrained-device exception'],[
('A security change would block the operator’s required emergency interaction with a physical process. The safety analysis requires that interaction to remain available. Which constraint governs the design?', 'The validated safety response must remain available while security controls are redesigned around it. A generic access restriction cannot override the process safety requirement.'),
('A required OT update involves a reboot that would interrupt an active process. Testing is complete and the process can safely stop during a planned outage. What should be arranged?', 'Use a controlled maintenance window coordinated with operations. A technically correct update can still be unsafe at the wrong operational time.'),
('A controller is to be taken offline under an approved procedure that depends on a standby path. Before the planned switchover, what should be confirmed?', 'Verify that the redundant path can safely assume its required function. The existence of a standby label is not evidence of readiness.'),
('An embedded sensor cannot support the standard endpoint agent. A risk owner approves specific network protections and a review date while replacement is planned. What governance record is needed?', 'Document the exception, constraints, controls and review boundary. Treating the device as fully compliant would hide the known limitation.')])
family(['Add an idempotency check','Require approval for high impact','Validate the event authenticity','Constrain the automation identity'],[
('A remediation webhook is delivered twice. The second execution duplicates an irreversible business-side action. Which workflow property is needed to handle retries safely?', 'Idempotency or deduplication ensures repeated delivery does not repeat the same action. Authenticity validation does not itself prevent duplicate valid events.'),
('An automated playbook can isolate a hospital’s shared identity service based on a low-confidence signal. Policy requires an authorized human decision for that business impact. Which gate is missing?', 'A human approval gate should precede that high-impact action under the stated policy. Faster execution does not compensate for insufficient authorization.'),
('A remediation endpoint accepts externally supplied events without checking their authenticated source. Which validation should occur before trusting an event to trigger action?', 'Authenticate and validate the event source and integrity. A least-privilege executor can still perform harmful permitted actions on forged input.'),
('A playbook needs to quarantine one endpoint but executes with unrestricted tenant administration rights. Which change reduces the authority available if the workflow is abused?', 'Use a narrowly scoped automation identity. Input validation is useful but does not justify unnecessary permissions.')])
family(['Evaluate the proposed configuration','Detect divergence from the baseline','Apply the approved correction','Verify the resulting service state'],[
('An infrastructure change is under review and has not been deployed. The team wants to identify prohibited settings before they reach production. Which automation stage fits?', 'Evaluate the proposed configuration before deployment. Runtime drift detection applies after actual state exists.'),
('A production resource differs from its approved infrastructure definition after a manual console change. Which capability first identifies this discrepancy?', 'Drift detection compares actual state with the approved baseline. A successful original deployment does not guarantee continuing consistency.'),
('A detected configuration deviation has an approved, tested remediation and a permitted change window. Which workflow step restores the intended setting?', 'Apply the authorized correction. Detection alone reports the deviation without changing it.'),
('Automation reports that a correction command returned success. The team must confirm both compliance and continued application operation. Which step completes the control loop?', 'Verify resulting configuration and service health. Command success does not prove the intended outcome or absence of unintended effects.')])
family(['Authenticated payload encryption','A publisher digital signature','A protected password hash','A tokenized business identifier'],[
('A message payload must remain secret and detect unauthorized alteration under an established symmetric key. Which mechanism best addresses both needs?', 'Authenticated encryption provides confidentiality and integrity under the key. A signature alone leaves the message readable.'),
('A distributor publishes a readable software package and needs customers to verify its origin and integrity using a trusted public key. Which mechanism fits?', 'A publisher signature provides origin and integrity evidence without requiring the package to be secret. A shared password hash is unrelated.'),
('A login service needs to verify passwords without retaining a reversibly encrypted copy. Which storage mechanism is appropriate?', 'Use a suitable salted, deliberately expensive password-hashing scheme. Reversible encryption creates a recovery path the verifier does not need.'),
('A business wants routine systems to use a substitute identifier while a tightly controlled service maintains the association with the original sensitive value. Which mechanism fits?', 'Tokenization substitutes a reference value and restricts access to the mapping. It is not the same as making the original value publicly verifiable.')])
family(['Rewrap the data-encryption keys','Reencrypt the affected payloads','Generate a fresh data key','Retain required historical keys'],[
('An envelope-encryption system rotates its key-encryption key. Existing data keys are still approved and uncompromised. Which operation can update their wrapping without rewriting every data object?', 'Rewrap the data-encryption keys with the new key-encryption key. The payload can remain unchanged when its data key remains suitable.'),
('A data-encryption key is confirmed compromised. The organization must protect retained plaintext under a new uncompromised key. Which operation addresses the affected ciphertext going forward?', 'Reencrypt affected data under a new key and manage old exposure appropriately. Merely wrapping the compromised key differently does not change what it can decrypt.'),
('A new dataset must have an encryption boundary independent of existing datasets. Which action creates independent key material for that boundary?', 'Generate a fresh data key with an approved cryptographic random process. Rewrapping an existing shared key does not make the datasets cryptographically independent.'),
('A key rotation completes, but lawful retained archives still depend on old decryption keys. Those keys are not compromised. Which lifecycle requirement prevents accidental loss of access?', 'Retain needed historical keys under suitable protection until dependent data can be migrated or disposed of. Rotation is not automatic permission to destroy all earlier keys.')])
family(['Protect past session secrecy','Plan quantum-resistant key exchange','Increase password-guessing cost','Split control of key recovery'],[
('A system must prevent later theft of its long-term authentication key from revealing earlier captured session contents, assuming ephemeral secrets were properly erased. Which cryptographic property is sought?', 'Forward secrecy protects prior sessions against later long-term key compromise under its assumptions. It is not automatically resistance to a quantum attacker.'),
('An archive must remain confidential for decades, and an adversary may store encrypted traffic now for future quantum analysis. Which migration concern is most relevant?', 'Assess and plan quantum-resistant key establishment for the long confidentiality lifetime. Classical forward secrecy alone does not address a future quantum break of recorded key exchange.'),
('Attackers have obtained password-verifier records. The system wants each offline guess to require substantial computation and memory while keeping legitimate verification practical. Which technique addresses this?', 'A deliberately expensive password derivation scheme raises guessing cost. Splitting recovery authority does not strengthen each password guess operation.'),
('Policy requires that no single custodian can reconstruct a recovery key alone. Which cryptographic governance arrangement fits?', 'Threshold splitting can require multiple independent shares for reconstruction. Ordinary key rotation does not impose multiple-custodian control.')])
family(['Compute over protected ciphertext','Authenticate visible associated data','Establish both peers’ identities','Erase the protected decryption key'],[
('A selected cryptographic scheme permits a service to evaluate a supported function on encrypted inputs without decrypting them. Which capability is being used?', 'Homomorphic encryption supports specified computation over ciphertext. It has practical limits and is not the same as ordinary transport encryption.'),
('A message’s routing metadata must remain readable but be bound to its encrypted payload so alteration is detected. Which AEAD feature fits?', 'Associated data is authenticated while remaining unencrypted. Including it only outside the authentication boundary would not bind it to the payload.'),
('Two services require each endpoint to authenticate the other during channel establishment. Which authentication property is required?', 'Mutual authentication establishes both peer identities. Server-only authentication does not authenticate the client endpoint.'),
('A storage system meets the prerequisites for approved cryptographic sanitization, including exclusive effective encryption and protected key management. Which action makes the encrypted data inaccessible by that method?', 'Cryptographic erase destroys the necessary key material under the approved process. It is effective only when all relevant keys and copies are handled and the method’s prerequisites hold.')])
assert len(ITEMS)==76
